    "raw": "Given:\n- Speed in normal space: 2 billion miles per hour\n- Speed through a black hole: 3 times faster than normal space, so 6 billion miles per hour\n- Time in normal space: 7 hours\n- Time through a black hole: 2 hours\n\nTo find the total distance traveled, we calculate the distance for each segment of the journey and then sum them up.\n\n1. Distance in normal space:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 2 \\, \\text{billion miles/hour} \\times 7 \\, \\text{hours} = 14 \\, \\text{billion miles} \\]\n\n2. Distance through a black hole:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 6 \\, \\text{billion miles/hour} \\times 2 \\, \\text{hours} = 12 \\, \\text{billion miles} \\]\n\n3. Total distance:\n\\[ \\text{Total Distance} = 14 \\, \\text{billion miles} + 12 \\, \\text{billion miles} = 26 \\, \\text{billion miles} \\]\n\nFINAL: 26",
